] [17592186369283 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12a066d8-58b4-511c-9cb2-861f5afc7e73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369284 #edb/ref 1080 "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99c2fa33-7e84-5fa9-b445-20cdce34028b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109326" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the arc of the curve $x=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y}$ that lies between the lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59c768e0-123a-5f86-b9a6-1b397e77b597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${y}_{1}=1$ to ${y}_{2}=e.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y})=\\frac{{y}^{4}-4}{4{y}^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{\\frac{{y}^{8}+8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,y\\sqrt{\\frac{({y}^{4}+4)^{2}}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y(\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{4{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({y}^{3}+\\frac{4}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{(\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}+4-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}({e}^{4}+15).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cfb25814-53f0-5252-8e81-2248d22b22d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}+1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e775560f-3f4c-54be-841d-b0c3d21fd878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}-12)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32562cc2-5b04-5833-b156-51f71e7dd7ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371559 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\